    description:
      "Periodized resistance training produced greater one-repetition-maximum gains than non-periodized training across 18 studies (ES = 0.43), with undulating models, higher frequency and longer programs favoured. Block periodization was proposed to overcome the conflicting adaptations of mixed training and the difficulty of multi-peaking, while Kiely's critique argues training responses vary so much between individuals that generic planning templates should give way to responsive, monitored systems. The evidence that HRV-guided prescription can match or beat block periodization in well-trained cyclists, and that elite endurance training self-organises toward a polarized distribution, points the same way. This is the elite move because it is a system run over years with a coach who adjusts to your data; the boundary is that the periodization trials are mostly in untrained lifters and the individualized-systems literature is young.",
    action: "Hire or partner with a qualified coach, agree a 12-month plan built from 3–6 week blocks with one clear emphasis each, share your daily load, sleep and HRV log, and review and re-plan the next block together every month.",
